From eeca8042ca13a671a5fbc06623e40e5adb7077bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiaAI-Lab <mia.ailab1@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 16:46:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 19/25] glm cuda: the KV pool says what a held-back request
 waits for, once a wait; unit tests for E4M3 pages

Rank 0 logs one line when admission starts holding a request back (its prompt and reply tokens, the
pages it needs, free and reclaimable of the pool's total, or that every paged sequence is busy) and
one when it fits again. Unit tests: an E4M3 page beside DFlash2 holds a DSA layer's codes, scales and
pooled keys (580 B a token, no MTP part) with ls and pk placed after the codes; a request needing
more pages than the whole pool is admitted and refused with PoolTooSmall, taking nothing, also while
the pool is busy. The pages unit fixture now names the target head (it read undefined before).

---
 zig/build/glm_family_host.zig            |  2 +-
 zig/src/families/glm/cuda_lanes.zig      |  2 +-
 zig/src/families/glm/cuda_pages.zig      | 25 ++++++++++++++--
 zig/src/families/glm/cuda_pages_test.zig | 38 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 62 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

